# Example script for the dialogue engine (#54). Compile with parseScript() from src/dialogue/script.js.
tree crypto_tokens start=hello
vars trust=0

= hello guest
{name} jingles a hardware wallet at you. "Last Resort, right? You take tokens?"
? [crisis>=70] {name} isn't smiling. "Be quick. Have you seen the news?"
* Of course. Your keys, your bunker. -> keys {trait vain, trust +5}
* [rep>=40] Only from people I trust. And I trust you. -> keys {trust +10}
* [trait paranoid | heat<30] Cash is better. Untraceable. -> cash {flag cash_deal}
* Tokens are a fad. Concrete isn't. -> rebuffed {aggressive}

= keys guest
"Good. I want a vault for the cold wallets. Under the vault. Under the pool."
* [trust>=10] A vault under a vault. I'll draw it tonight. -> win {promise wine_cellar, trust +5}
* Let's talk about the air first. -> air once {trust +2}
* [crisis>=45] The way things are going, you'll want it by spring. -> win_fear {fear $guest}

= air guest
"Air? Sure. Scrubbers, whatever. Back to the vault."
* Fine. The vault. -> keys
* Everyone forgets the air until the door shuts. -> win_fear {fear $guest, learn paranoid}

= cash guest
> {heat +1}
"Untraceable. I like you." {name} lowers their voice.
* Between us? We hear about these things early. -> win_tip {slip}
* Just good practice. -> win {trust +3}

= win !sold_dream
{name} sends a deposit before the canapes come round.
= win_fear !sold_fear
{name} pockets your card. "Send the air numbers."
= win_tip !insider_tip
{name} goes pale and reaches for a pen.
= rebuffed !rebuffed
"A fad." {name} turns back to the bar.
